i-nu\">Yang-chi-nu</a></div><div class=\"wst-header-forward-arrow\">\u2192</div></div></div><div class=\"wst-header-notes header&#95;notes searchaux wst-unknown-notes\"><style data-mw-deduplicate=\"TemplateStyles:r14791120\">.mw-parser-output .plainSister{display:block;font-size:93%;line-height:normal;list-style-type:none;list-style-image:none;list-style-position:outside;border:1px solid var(--border-color-interactive--hover,#AAA);float:right;clear:right;margin:0.5ex 0 0.5ex 0.5ex;padding:0;background:var(--background-color-base,#FFFFFF);color:var(--color-base,#202122)}.mw-parser-output .sisicon,.mw-parser-output .dabicon{padding-right:1ex}</style><ul class=\"plainSister\"><li class=\"sisitem\"><span class=\"sisicon\"><span typeof=\"mw:File/Frameless\"><a href=\"/wiki/Special:SiteMatrix\" title=\"Special:SiteMatrix\"><img alt=\"Sister Projects\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/Wikimedia-logo.svg/20px-Wikimedia-logo.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikisource.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"18\" height=\"18\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/Wikimedia-logo.svg/40px-Wikimedia-logo.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikisource.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" data-file-width=\"1024\" data-file-height=\"1024\" /></a></span></span><a href=\"/wiki/Special:SiteMatrix\" title=\"Special:SiteMatrix\">sister projects</a>: <a href=\"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q107367909\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"d:Q107367909\">Wikidata item</a></li></ul></div><div class=\"ws-noexport\" id=\"ws-data\" style=\"speak:none\"><span id=\"ws-article-id\">3678066</span><span id=\"ws-title\"><a href=\"/wiki/Eminent_Chinese_of_the_Ch%27ing_Period\" title=\"Eminent Chinese of the Ch&#39;ing Period\">Eminent Chinese of the Ch'ing Period</a>, Volume 2 \u2014 Wu Yen</span><span id=\"ws-editor\">Arthur W. Hummel</span><span id=\"ws-author\">Fang Chao-ying</span></div></div>\n<p><span style=\"display:none\" id=\"dynamic&#95;layout&#95;overrider\">Layout 2</span>\n</p>\n<div class=\"prp-pages-output\" lang=\"en\">\n<p><span><span class=\"pagenum ws-pagenum\" id=\"883\" data-page-number=\"883\" data-page-name=\"Page:Eminent Chinese Of The Ch\u2019ing Period - Hummel - 1943 - Vol. 2.pdf/281\" data-page-index=\"281\" data-page-quality=\"3\" title=\"Page:Eminent&#95;Chinese&#95;Of&#95;The&#95;Ch%E2%80%99ing&#95;Period&#95;-&#95;Hummel&#95;-&#95;1943&#95;-&#95;Vol.&#95;2.pdf/281\"><span id=\"pageindex&#95;281\" class=\"pagenum-inner ws-noexport\">&#8203;</span></span></span><b>WU</b> Yen \u5433\u708e (<style data-mw-deduplicate=\"TemplateStyles:r14767791\">.mw-parser-output .wst-tooltip{cursor:help;border-bottom:thin dotted cornflowerblue}.mw-parser-output .wst-tooltip-nodash{border-bottom:none}</style><span class=\"wst-tooltip wst-tooltip-dash\" title=\"Courtesy name (Tz\u00fb/Zi, \u5b57)\">T.</span>&#160;\u8d64\u6e9f[\u6c11],&#32;<link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r14767791\" /><span class=\"wst-tooltip wst-tooltip-dash\" title=\"Literary name (Hao, \u865f)\">H.</span>&#160;\u5abf\u5eb5), d. July 1, 1663, age forty (<i>sui</i>), historian, was a native of Wu-chiang, Kiangsu. He and <span class=\"ws-authlkpl\"><a href=\"/wiki/Eminent_Chinese_of_the_Ch%27ing_Period/P%27an_Ch%27%C3%AAng-chang\" title=\"Eminent Chinese of the Ch&#39;ing Period/P&#39;an Ch&#39;\u00eang-chang\">P'an Ch'\u00eang-chang</a></span>&#32;[<i>q.&#8239;v.</i>] were co-authors of a history of the Ming dynasty and of a poetical account of that dynasty, the latter completed in 1656 under the title \u4eca\u6a02\u5e9c <i>Chin y\u00fceh-fu</i>. Both works were ordered by imperial decree to be destroyed, but the second of the two endured and was reprinted in the <i>Yin-li tsai-ss\u016d t'ang ts'ung-shu</i> (see under <span class=\"ws-authlkpl\"><a href=\"/wiki/Eminent_Chinese_of_the_Ch%27ing_Period/Chu_Y%C3%BCn\" title=\"Eminent Chinese of the Ch&#39;ing Period/Chu Y\u00fcn\">Chu Y\u00fcn</a></span>). Wu was involved as one of the assistant compilers of <span class=\"ws-authlkpl\"><a href=\"/wiki/Eminent_Chinese_of_the_Ch%27ing_Period/Chuang_T%27ing-lung\" title=\"Eminent Chinese of the Ch&#39;ing Period/Chuang T&#39;ing-lung\">Chuang T'ing-lung's</a></span>&#32;[<i>q.&#8239;v.</i>] banned work, <i>Ming-shih chi-l\u00fceh</i>, and was put to death at Hangchow in July 1663.\n</p>\n<style data-mw-deduplicate=\"TemplateStyles:r15431518\">.mw-parser-output .wst-rule{background-color:currentcolor;color:inherit;width:auto;margin:2px auto 2px auto;height:1px;overflow:hidden}.mw-parser-output .wst-rule.wst-rule-left{margin-left:0}.mw-parser-output .wst-rule.wst-rule-right{margin-right:0}.mw-parser-output .wst-rule.__uirule{background-color:#a2a9b1;color:inherit;border:0;margin-top:0.2em;margin-bottom:0.2em}</style><hr class=\"wst-rule wst-rule-left\" style=\"color:inherit;width:40%;\" />\n<p>[6/35/23b\u201328b; <i>T'oung Pao</i> 1928\u201329, p. 416, for note on above <i>ts'ung-shu</i>.]\n</p>\n<style data-mw-deduplicate=\"TemplateStyles:r15431519\">.mw-parser-output .wst-right{text-align:right}</style><div class=\"wst-right\" style=\"margin-right:2em;\">\n<p><span class=\"smallcaps\" style=\"font-variant:small-caps;\">Fang Chao-ying</span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<p><br />\n&#32;\n</p>\n</div>\n</div>"},"links":[{"ns":0,"exists":"","*":"Eminent Chinese of the Ch'ing Period"},{"ns":0,"exists":"","*":"Eminent Chinese of the Ch'ing Period/Chu Y\u00fcn"},{"ns":0,"exists":"","*":"Eminent Chinese of the Ch'ing Period/Chuang T'ing-lung"},{"ns":0,"exists":"","*":"Eminent Chinese of the Ch'ing Period/P'an Ch'\u00eang-chang"},{"ns":0,"exists":"","*":"Eminent Chinese of the Ch'ing Period/Wu-ya"},{"ns":0,"exists":"","*":"Eminent Chinese of the Ch'ing Period/Yang-chi-nu"},{"ns":102,"exists":"","*":"Author:Arthur W. Hummel"},{"ns":102,"exists":"","*":"Author:Fang Chao-ying"}],"sections":[],"wikitext":{"*":"{{Eminent 